WEBVTT

00:15.100 --> 00:21.910
Kokoro no mori no naka kimi ni deau koto

00:15.100 --> 00:21.910
I was always dreaming of meeting you

00:16.100 --> 00:22.150
<b>Zettai Shonen</b>

00:21.910 --> 00:26.980
Itsumo yume mitetan da

00:21.910 --> 00:26.980
within my heart’s forest.

00:26.980 --> 00:33.120
Hikari no silhouette sono saki wo mezashite

00:26.980 --> 00:33.120
The silhouette of light guides the way.

00:33.120 --> 00:38.750
Itsuka ai ni furete mitai

00:33.120 --> 00:38.750
One day, I’d like to try and experience love.

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
Kimochi to kotoba niji to mizutamari

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
My feelings and words can be like rainbows and puddles.

00:44.460 --> 00:51.870
Omoiau yasashisa ga michibiku ashita he to

00:44.460 --> 00:51.870
The kindness we share will guide us into tomorrow.

00:51.870 --> 00:57.370
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru kara

00:51.870 --> 00:57.370
With only you here, I can become stronger.

00:57.370 --> 01:03.670
Sora takaku negai wo kanadeyou

00:57.370 --> 01:03.670
My wish will be granted in the heights of the sky.

01:03.670 --> 01:09.050
Nanika taisetsu ka wo miushinawanu you ni

01:03.670 --> 01:09.050
You won’t lose sight of something precious to you,

01:09.050 --> 01:18.320
Kitto motto kagayaku kara

01:09.050 --> 01:18.320
because I’m sure it’ll shine even brighter.

01:18.320 --> 01:23.770
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru no sa

01:18.320 --> 01:23.770
With only you here, I can become stronger.

01:23.770 --> 01:30.130
Ima dekiru koto kara hajimeyou

01:23.770 --> 01:30.130
Let’s start with what we can do right now.

01:30.130 --> 01:35.510
Mawarimichi demo ii jibun wo shinjite

01:30.130 --> 01:35.510
I don’t mind if we take a detour, 
as long as you believe in yourself.

01:35.510 --> 01:44.620
Kitto motto sono saki he to

01:35.510 --> 01:44.620
By doing that, I’m sure we can go even further.

01:56.930 --> 01:59.570
<b>Why is it called “Touya,” anyway?</b>

01:59.570 --> 02:01.870
<b>I’d understand if it was called the Lord’s Forest...</b>

02:01.870 --> 02:04.310
<b>...but I’ve never heard of a “Touya” before...</b>

02:04.310 --> 02:06.940
<b>So I was wondering why it was
called the “Touya Forest.”</b>

02:06.940 --> 02:08.980
<b>So that’s what you meant.</b>

02:08.980 --> 02:11.450
<b>A lord and a Touya are completely different.</b>

02:11.450 --> 02:13.110
<b>You said you could understand
if it was a “lord’s,” right?</b>

02:13.120 --> 02:17.890
<b>In present day terms... it pretty much
refers to a village leader, right?</b>

02:17.890 --> 02:18.390
<b>Right.</b>

02:18.390 --> 02:22.220
<b>I guess you could say the lord would
be the town’s administrator.</b>

02:22.220 --> 02:27.130
<b>And his counterpart, the Touya, would
organize or sponsor the festivals.</b>

02:27.130 --> 02:31.270
<b>Normally, he’d be a priest or a very devout
person and act as the religious leader.</b>

02:33.740 --> 02:36.800
<b>Usually, the Touya would just do his rounds
at predetermined times, but...</b>

02:36.810 --> 02:39.340
<b>...here, both roles were running
concurrently all the time...</b>

02:39.340 --> 02:43.440
<b>...and it turns out that the Touya
was actually the one on top.</b>

02:43.450 --> 02:44.650
<b>I guess that’s about it.</b>

02:44.650 --> 02:47.250
<b>So the village leader was a Shinto priest?</b>

02:47.250 --> 02:49.920
<b>A Shinto priest is a little different.</b>

02:49.920 --> 02:51.420
<b>How can I explain it...</b>

02:55.260 --> 02:56.160
<b>Thanks for the meal.</b>

02:56.160 --> 02:59.060
<b>Oh, could you open the vet for me?</b>

02:59.060 --> 03:00.290
<b>Sure.</b>

