03:23.090 --> 03:24.450
<b>Welcome.</b>

03:28.260 --> 03:29.190
<b>Asako-san.</b>

03:30.130 --> 03:33.160
<b>Do you know if the Cat Dance and the
Touya Forest are connected somehow?</b>

03:33.160 --> 03:34.600
<b>That came out of nowhere.</b>

03:34.600 --> 03:35.930
<b>Sorry.</b>

03:36.470 --> 03:38.900
<b>You don’t have to apologize.</b>

03:38.900 --> 03:40.600
<b>A connection, huh?</b>

03:40.600 --> 03:41.900
<b>So are they?</b>

03:41.900 --> 03:46.210
<b>Well... the Cat Dance is a festival that started around the end of the Showa period in 1989...</b>

03:47.110 --> 03:51.350
<b>And nobody lived in the Touya Forest by then, so...</b>

03:51.350 --> 03:53.480
<b>I thought it was a much older festival...</b>

03:53.480 --> 03:56.720
<b>To be honest, I think it was made
just to wake this town up a little.</b>

04:01.360 --> 04:02.520
<b>Is something wrong?</b>

04:04.030 --> 04:04.930
<b>No...</b>

04:20.510 --> 04:21.480
<b>Wait up!</b>

04:21.480 --> 04:22.780
<b>Aizawa!</b>

04:23.610 --> 04:24.510
<b>Wait a sec!</b>

04:27.780 --> 04:29.480
<b>What?</b>

04:29.480 --> 04:34.260
<b>[ Sakakura Motors ]</b>

04:35.990 --> 04:36.490
<b>Here.</b>

04:40.200 --> 04:43.000
<b>You were going up the
Nakizawagawa River again, weren’t you?</b>

04:44.030 --> 04:45.600
<b>It has nothing to do with you.</b>

04:45.600 --> 04:46.730
<b>It does!</b>

04:46.740 --> 04:48.240
<b>It really does.</b>

04:49.770 --> 04:51.970
<b>What do you think of that place?</b>

04:51.970 --> 04:53.370
<b>What do you mean?</b>

04:53.380 --> 04:55.510
<b>Do you think there are really kappas there?</b>

04:57.880 --> 04:59.650
<b>Be honest.</b>

04:59.650 --> 05:03.780
<b>When someone says “kappa,” I imagine
one living in a deep, bottomless pool...</b>

05:06.220 --> 05:09.320
<b>But it’s not like that up there, right?</b>

05:09.320 --> 05:10.860
<b>It’s impossible.</b>

05:10.860 --> 05:11.560
<b>What is?</b>

05:11.560 --> 05:14.100
<b>Kappas don’t live up there.</b>

05:14.100 --> 05:17.160
<b>Then, Aizawa... why are you always
coming and going from there?</b>

05:18.970 --> 05:21.070
<b>I know, too...</b>

05:22.140 --> 05:24.670
<b>I know there’s no sign of kappas up there...</b>

05:24.670 --> 05:26.240
<b>But what should I do?</b>

05:26.240 --> 05:28.240
<b>I did see one.</b>

05:29.680 --> 05:31.610
<b>You saw something too,
didn’t you, Aizawa?</b>

05:40.890 --> 05:41.490
<b>Umm...</b>

05:41.490 --> 05:42.760
<b>It’s all right.</b>

05:42.760 --> 05:44.530
<b>You don’t have to say anything.</b>

05:44.530 --> 05:46.960
<b>That’s a better way of doing things anyway.</b>

05:46.960 --> 05:49.500
<b>I told everyone, and now they
look at me like I’m a fool...</b>

05:50.370 --> 05:51.970
<b>My parents, my friends...</b>

05:51.970 --> 05:53.970
<b>Everyone’s laughed at me.</b>

05:54.970 --> 05:57.810
<b>The only one who hasn’t laughed at me is Miyama.</b>

05:57.810 --> 05:59.940
<b>Ah, Miki, that is.</b>

05:59.940 --> 06:00.440
<b>Yeah...</b>

06:01.380 --> 06:02.810
<b>After so much time has passed...</b>

06:02.810 --> 06:09.050
<b>...it’s hard to separate what I actually saw from what my own wild imagination made up.</b>

06:09.050 --> 06:13.650
<b>I’ll never forget the faces of those
who made fun of me, though.</b>

06:13.660 --> 06:16.760
<b>I definitely saw Old Lady Okaka fighting with a kappa.</b>

06:16.760 --> 06:19.990
<b>And she’s clearly missing an ear now.</b>

06:20.000 --> 06:22.930
<b>Ah, yeah, about Old Lady Okaka...</b>

06:22.930 --> 06:27.640
<b>You know how they say cats and dogs
can see things humans can’t, right?</b>

06:27.640 --> 06:31.970
<b>We might’ve just seen something
like that for a split second.</b>

06:32.870 --> 06:34.110
<b>Aren’t you going to eat that?</b>

06:34.110 --> 06:34.940
<b>You want it?</b>

06:37.950 --> 06:38.980
<b>But you know...</b>

06:38.980 --> 06:42.120
<b>Didn’t you say Old Lady Okaka was your rival?</b>

06:42.120 --> 06:44.690
<b>It’s easier to explain things
to people that way, isn’t it?</b>

06:47.220 --> 06:47.920
<b>Long ago...</b>

06:49.190 --> 06:50.320
<b>Over there...</b>

06:50.330 --> 06:51.160
<b>Where?</b>

06:51.790 --> 06:56.460
<b>Why did you stop me from going
into the Touya Forest back then?</b>

06:56.470 --> 06:58.270
<b>If you’re looking for an explanation...</b>

06:58.270 --> 07:00.130
<b>...<i>he</i> knows a lot about it.</b>

07:27.960 --> 07:31.600
<b>\hShione here. ^_^
Today’s pretty hot again, huh?
How are your studies going?</b>

07:49.420 --> 07:50.450
<b>Do you need something?</b>

07:54.890 --> 07:58.360
<b>Kaburaki</b>

08:01.060 --> 08:03.760
<b>Your room’s sure in an interesting place, huh?</b>

08:03.770 --> 08:05.800
<b>It’s a servant’s room.</b>

08:06.840 --> 08:09.800
<b>Long ago, they had the livestock live
in the same room as the people.</b>

08:10.810 --> 08:13.110
<b>I guess you could say it’s my resistance to this place.</b>

08:13.110 --> 08:16.110
<b>Because I don’t like being the eldest son
following the path of those who used to live here.</b>

08:18.810 --> 08:21.150
<b>So, you wanted to know about
the Touya Forest, right?</b>

08:21.150 --> 08:21.780
<b>Yeah.</b>

08:22.620 --> 08:24.420
<b>Around the 40th year of the Showa period, 1966...</b>

08:24.420 --> 08:29.090
<b>...in order to improve the country’s rice paddies, the government dug up lots of places.</b>

08:29.090 --> 08:30.590
<b>But at the time...</b>

08:30.590 --> 08:34.730
<b>...even the largest earth-moving machines
couldn’t deal with the giant Japanese cedar trees...</b>

08:34.730 --> 08:36.860
<b>...which showed up everywhere they went.</b>

08:36.870 --> 08:39.470
<b>Umm... then that’s...?</b>

08:39.470 --> 08:41.770
<b>Wait until I’m done.
There’s a proper sequence to things.</b>

08:45.370 --> 08:47.480
<b>And since that happened...</b>

08:47.480 --> 08:52.050
<b>...most of the area in the valley that used
to be forest was turned into a lake.</b>

08:52.050 --> 08:54.580
<b>Due to the ash and lava from Mt. Fuji’s old eruptions,</b>

08:54.580 --> 08:56.680
<b>this land was formed as you see it today.</b>

08:56.690 --> 09:02.720
<b>Only the Touya Forest was left as an island
back when this area was still just a lake.</b>

09:04.030 --> 09:07.700
<b>Originally, that place was the center of the valley...</b>

09:07.700 --> 09:09.700
<b>...so it was considered to be a special location.</b>

09:09.700 --> 09:13.830
<b>Still... you can’t really tell why it’s
special with just that, right?</b>

09:13.840 --> 09:16.540
<b>To tell you the truth,
I’m not too sure myself.</b>

09:17.610 --> 09:21.480
<b>But don’t you get the feeling that a place might be special if a ton of trees suddenly grow...</b>

09:21.480 --> 09:23.810
<b>...and fill up an island in the middle of a lake?</b>

09:26.580 --> 09:28.950
<b>I guess I might feel that it’s kind of mysterious...</b>

09:31.920 --> 09:35.860
<b>It’s like the feeling you get when you
enter the grounds of a large shrine.</b>

09:35.860 --> 09:40.060
<b>You don’t know why, but you feel thankful for
its existence, and it gives you peace of mind.</b>

09:40.060 --> 09:41.400
<b>Ah... yeah.</b>

09:42.060 --> 09:46.370
<b>That abandoned house at its entrance
used to be called the Moriya.</b>

09:46.870 --> 09:49.040
<b>It’s written with the characters
Mori (protect) and Ya (valley).</b>

09:49.040 --> 09:53.340
<b>Since long ago, that house is said
to have protected this valley.</b>

09:53.880 --> 09:55.310
<b>But that’s...</b>

09:57.250 --> 09:59.810
<b>They don’t mean it’s protecting against
outside enemies, do they?</b>

10:01.450 --> 10:02.780
<b>Why do you say that?</b>

10:03.250 --> 10:07.420
<b>If that’s how it was, they would have
called that area the “Moriya Forest.”</b>

10:07.420 --> 10:10.220
<b>I can’t figure out why it was called the “Touya Forest.”</b>

10:10.230 --> 10:12.730
<b>You... sure are an interesting guy.</b>

10:14.060 --> 10:15.760
<b>This may or may not be the case, but...</b>

10:16.670 --> 10:18.160
<b>...that special forest has probably been...</b>

10:18.160 --> 10:21.070
<b>...protecting something even more special inside of it.</b>

10:22.140 --> 10:25.440
<b>So the procedure of protecting it probably
turned into a ceremony or festival...</b>

10:25.440 --> 10:27.680
<b>...and Moriya changed to Touya.</b>

10:27.680 --> 10:29.480
<b>So what could it be protecting...?</b>

10:29.480 --> 10:31.050
<b>Who knows?</b>

10:32.350 --> 10:33.450
<b>By the way...</b>

10:37.920 --> 10:41.060
<b>What do you think of Miyama Miki?</b>

10:41.060 --> 10:42.260
<b>What do I think of her?</b>

10:43.530 --> 10:44.660
<b>Nothing much.</b>

10:44.660 --> 10:45.630
<b>I see.</b>

10:45.630 --> 10:46.630
<b>Then I guess things are fine.</b>

10:47.630 --> 10:52.130
<b>And in the end, you’ll be gone with
your summer vacation, anyway.</b>

10:53.370 --> 10:54.870
<b>What’s that supposed to mean?</b>

10:55.570 --> 10:58.840
<b>Aizawa-kun, this isn’t the place
where you belong, is it?</b>

11:36.780 --> 11:39.810
<b>Umm... if you’re looking for Miku,
she’s no here right now.</b>

11:40.480 --> 11:41.680
<b>No, that’s not it...</b>

11:45.650 --> 11:47.990
<b>I’m sorry. It’s nothing.</b>

11:47.990 --> 11:49.120
<b>Wait.</b>

11:49.730 --> 11:51.930
<b>Aizawa-kun, wait here a sec, okay?</b>

11:54.130 --> 11:55.430
<b>You better wait, okay?</b>

12:31.930 --> 12:34.900
<b>When did the Cat Dance start?</b>

12:34.900 --> 12:35.870
<b>Yeah.</b>

12:35.870 --> 12:39.970
<b>Let’s see... I’d say it probably started
a little less than twenty years ago.</b>

12:39.980 --> 12:41.280
<b>That’s it.</b>

12:41.280 --> 12:44.910
<b>Since long ago, this street has been
called Nekogatsuji (Cats’ Crossing)...</b>

12:44.910 --> 12:46.780
<b>...and cats have been dancing
here since the Edo period.</b>

12:46.780 --> 12:49.420
<b>Nekogatsuji
Street</b>

12:47.320 --> 12:49.420
<b>What? They’ve been dancing?</b>

12:49.420 --> 12:52.690
<b>I think it was during the Tenpo period...</b>

12:52.690 --> 12:56.660
<b>You mean the same Tenpo from the
Tenpo Reforms started by Mizuno Tadakuni?</b>

12:56.660 --> 12:57.390
<b>Right, right.</b>

12:57.390 --> 13:01.430
<b>There’s a story from back then of
Nekogatsuji Street acting as a stage.</b>

13:04.770 --> 13:06.660
<b>Mr. So-and-So,
one of the Moriya’s servants,</b>

13:06.660 --> 13:08.970
<b>was walking home after finishing some errands.</b>

13:08.970 --> 13:13.670
<b>Just as he happened to approach
this area, he heard some voices.</b>

13:13.680 --> 13:14.840
<b>There were several voices.</b>

13:16.140 --> 13:18.050
<b>“Ah, he’s finally come!”</b>

13:18.050 --> 13:19.880
<b>“You’re late, Shiro!”</b>

13:19.880 --> 13:22.820
<b>“We can’t start dancing until you come, Shiro!”</b>

13:22.820 --> 13:25.720
<b>“Now, now. Tora, Buchi, Tama...”</b>

13:25.720 --> 13:28.460
<b>“...Shiro’s here now, so it’s okay.”</b>

13:29.320 --> 13:32.930
<b>Even though the servant heard the voices,
he wasn’t able to see anyone...</b>

13:32.930 --> 13:35.700
<b>...because the area was thick with foliage.</b>

13:35.700 --> 13:39.930
<b>“Is this the doing of a raccoon? I won’t be fooled!”</b>

13:39.940 --> 13:42.140
<b>And so Mr. So-and-So silently
moved towards the voices.</b>

13:42.700 --> 13:45.270
<b>“Come on, Shiro! Hurry and play your flute for us!”</b>

13:45.270 --> 13:48.840
<b>“Yeah! Let’s dance! Let’s dance!”</b>

13:48.840 --> 13:51.250
<b>But that’s when Shiro said...</b>

13:51.250 --> 13:55.050
<b>“My master fed me some hot food...”</b>

13:55.050 --> 13:57.250
<b>“...so I burned the end of my tongue.”</b>

13:57.250 --> 13:59.120
<b>“I can’t play my flute tonight.”</b>

14:00.990 --> 14:02.360
<b>They were cats!</b>

14:02.360 --> 14:03.860
<b>After he learned that...</b>

14:03.860 --> 14:07.290
<b>...he realized the cat named Shiro
was the one living in the Moriya.</b>

14:07.300 --> 14:09.400
<b>How mysterious that
things like this happen.</b>

14:10.070 --> 14:14.540
<b>When Mr. So-and-So returned home,
he reported what had happened to his master.</b>

14:14.540 --> 14:16.370
<b>The master was shocked.</b>

14:16.370 --> 14:19.910
<b>“It is true that I did indeed feed Shiro...”</b>

14:19.910 --> 14:23.740
<b>“...but then he went into a frenzy and ran off...”</b>

14:23.750 --> 14:27.010
<b>“This is terrible. It looks like I’ve
been keeping a demon cat...”</b>

14:27.020 --> 14:30.350
<b>“I wonder if there’s anything I can do to get rid of it.”</b>

14:30.850 --> 14:34.820
<b>In the end, the master left that duty to Mr. So-and-So.</b>

14:34.820 --> 14:36.500
<b>Unable to think of anything else,</b>

14:36.500 --> 14:39.630
<b>Mr. So-and-So approached Shiro directly and spoke with him.</b>

14:39.630 --> 14:41.830
<b>“The reason we’re keeping you in our house...”</b>

14:41.830 --> 14:45.330
<b>“...isn’t so you can play your flute or dance.”</b>

14:46.000 --> 14:51.110
<b>“If you’re really doing that, then
we can’t let you remain here.”</b>

14:51.110 --> 14:53.340
<b>“Please go somewhere else.”</b>

15:01.780 --> 15:06.820
<b>And since that day, it’s said that the cat
Shiro was never seen there again.</b>

15:12.630 --> 15:14.500
<b>That sure is a weird story.</b>

15:14.500 --> 15:17.230
<b>I wonder why Shiro left so obediently like that.</b>

15:17.800 --> 15:19.070
<b>Well...</b>

15:19.070 --> 15:22.440
<b>Isn’t it the same as the crane woman in “The Crane’s Gratitude,”</b>

15:22.440 --> 15:23.840
<b>whose true identity was revealed?</b>

15:23.840 --> 15:26.970
<b>But in the crane woman’s case, they had already made a promise about it earlier, right?</b>

15:26.980 --> 15:28.610
<b>Ah, that’s right.</b>

15:28.610 --> 15:30.580
<b>“Please don’t look.”</b>

15:30.580 --> 15:32.100
<b>Don’t you think the story of Shiro</b>

15:32.100 --> 15:34.950
<b>is somewhat broken in comparison to normal old stories like that?</b>

15:34.950 --> 15:35.950
<b>I don’t know.</b>

15:36.490 --> 15:39.120
<b>Because we think it’s a tale...</b>

15:39.120 --> 15:43.920
<b>...or maybe just a story, we might expect
it to have a sensible ending.</b>

15:45.160 --> 15:48.030
<b>The old tales we know...</b>

15:48.030 --> 15:51.170
<b>...or rather, all the old tales that
have been passed down....</b>

15:51.170 --> 15:54.340
<b>...have survived through hundreds of years.</b>

15:55.000 --> 16:01.210
<b>And since they’re stories, I think they’ve all had things added or changes applied to them.</b>

16:01.210 --> 16:03.240
<b>So... as for the story you just told me...</b>

16:03.250 --> 16:08.080
<b>...if it’s really in its original form,
don’t you think that’s all right?</b>

16:08.080 --> 16:10.120
<b>Its original form, huh?</b>

16:10.120 --> 16:13.920
<b>And it was still called Moriya and
not Touya back then, huh?</b>

16:13.920 --> 16:16.560
<b>You’re right! I didn’t even realize.</b>

16:38.850 --> 16:40.850
<b>You’re not going to run from me today?</b>

16:50.490 --> 16:52.530
<b>I haven’t shown you this yet, right?</b>

16:56.730 --> 16:58.530
<b>This is...?</b>

16:58.530 --> 16:59.830
<b>Look closer.</b>

17:05.310 --> 17:06.470
<b>CG?</b>

17:06.480 --> 17:07.840
<b>Why would I do that?</b>

17:07.840 --> 17:08.640
<b>No idea.</b>

17:09.380 --> 17:13.110
<b>I think you and Unno-san have also seen this thing.</b>

17:13.120 --> 17:14.720
<b>It’s fine if you think that...</b>

17:14.720 --> 17:17.790
<b>...but it’s a problem if you go around telling everyone that because of your selfish thoughts.</b>

17:17.790 --> 17:21.190
<b>Oh... I wasn’t planning on going anywhere with it.</b>

17:21.190 --> 17:24.790
<b>Is that so? Then isn’t it fine leaving things at that?</b>

17:24.790 --> 17:25.630
<b>You’re also...</b>

17:27.160 --> 17:30.100
<b>...looking for the way out, aren’t you?</b>

17:30.100 --> 17:31.800
<b>Because...</b>

17:31.800 --> 17:35.570
<b>...you want to believe that this world
is an open place, don’t you?</b>

17:37.610 --> 17:40.040
<b>Have you heard of fairy rings?</b>

17:40.780 --> 17:41.880
<b>In England...</b>

17:41.880 --> 17:46.150
<b>...they’re mushroom-filled paths that have
grown in a circular fashion in a field.</b>

17:46.150 --> 17:52.090
<b>The people over there thought they
were left behind by dancing fairies.</b>

17:52.090 --> 17:53.620
<b>They thought that for a very long time.</b>

17:54.220 --> 17:59.490
<b>Recent research has shown that fungus,
or something related to mushrooms...</b>

17:59.490 --> 18:01.680
<b>...spreads its spores into the ground</b>

18:01.680 --> 18:04.200
<b>and makes the circular pattern in the grass looking for food.</b>

18:04.200 --> 18:05.870
<b>So now we know that fairies never existed?</b>

18:05.870 --> 18:06.600
<b>Yes! That’s exactly it!</b>

18:07.740 --> 18:09.340
<b>I wonder if that’s really the case, though.</b>

18:09.870 --> 18:13.070
<b>Fairy rings are not circles that
fairies have danced around.</b>

18:13.080 --> 18:15.410
<b>That has indeed been proven.</b>

18:15.410 --> 18:20.080
<b>But just because of that,
people deny the existence of fairies.</b>

18:20.080 --> 18:21.820
<b>I think that’s wrong...</b>

18:21.820 --> 18:24.790
<b>Right! That’s what I want to say!</b>

18:25.490 --> 18:28.860
<b>What you can see is not all there is to this world.</b>

18:28.860 --> 18:31.660
<b>This world is definitely not as closed as that.</b>

18:31.660 --> 18:37.770
<b>The things we can’t perceive are just entangled within the many layers connected to them.</b>

18:38.270 --> 18:41.200
<b>I want to think that way.</b>

18:41.200 --> 18:44.170
<b>But couldn’t you say that’s an escapist attitude?</b>

18:44.170 --> 18:45.740
<b>You sure hit some painful points...</b>

18:46.340 --> 18:49.210
<b>I wouldn’t call it escapist so much
as a desire to understand.</b>

18:50.150 --> 18:53.010
<b>“Beyond that mountain lies an unknown city.”</b>

18:53.010 --> 18:56.020
<b>“Beyond the sea lies an unknown world.”</b>

18:56.020 --> 18:59.990
<b>Haven’t we managed to come this far because
people have thought that way?</b>

18:59.990 --> 19:05.230
<b>If all we see in this valley is all there is
to the world, I’ll be pretty depressed.</b>

19:20.640 --> 19:22.180
<b>What?</b>

19:22.180 --> 19:22.810
<b>Nothing...</b>

19:55.510 --> 19:56.940
<b>What is it?</b>

19:56.950 --> 19:59.010
<b>I want to talk.</b>

20:06.320 --> 20:07.520
<b>Don’t you have anything?</b>

20:07.520 --> 20:09.590
<b>What do you mean?</b>

20:09.590 --> 20:10.990
<b>Anything to talk about...</b>

20:12.430 --> 20:13.590
<b>Geez.</b>

20:18.170 --> 20:19.600
<b>Hey, Ayumu...</b>

20:22.940 --> 20:25.410
<b>Have you ever... kissed before?</b>

20:26.610 --> 20:27.940
<b>So you haven’t.</b>

20:28.940 --> 20:30.080
<b>Do you want to?</b>

20:35.880 --> 20:37.450
<b>Look at me.</b>

20:40.820 --> 20:44.360
<b>If you want to kiss me, you can.</b>

20:49.100 --> 20:52.000
<b>So a kiss is something you have
to get permission to do.</b>

20:52.000 --> 20:53.430
<b>What’s with that?</b>

20:53.440 --> 20:56.800
<b>I understand your feelings of not fitting in here.</b>

20:56.810 --> 20:58.270
<b>Because I’m also an outsider.</b>

20:59.070 --> 21:03.540
<b>But if you’re trying to find your place by simply becoming Kaburaki-kun’s girlfriend...</b>

21:03.550 --> 21:05.650
<b>...I think that’s wrong.</b>

21:05.650 --> 21:08.820
<b>And if you just want Kaburaki-kun’s attention
and want to make him jealous...</b>

21:08.820 --> 21:11.250
<b>...I think that’s even more wrong.</b>

21:13.220 --> 21:14.790
<b>Sorry.</b>

21:15.660 --> 21:17.690
<b>Don’t apologize! Stupid!</b>

21:35.280 --> 21:36.780
<b>Ah...</b>

22:05.210 --> 22:05.870
<b>Stop!</b>

22:12.280 --> 22:13.410
<b>Don’t go!</b>

22:14.180 --> 22:17.250
<b>You can’t go past there.</b>

22:18.050 --> 22:21.460
<b>If you go past there, you won’t be able to come back.</b>

22:21.460 --> 22:22.220
<b>Calm down.</b>

22:23.290 --> 22:25.460
<b>I won’t be able to come back...?</b>

22:25.460 --> 22:27.400
<b>I was told that back then, too...</b>

22:28.660 --> 22:30.930
<b>It was the same for me.</b>

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
Daremo shiranai kotoba de kimi he to

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
On that nostalgic hill, I sang out to you

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
Utaikaketa natsukashii oka de

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
words that no one else knew.

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
Tomare soyokaze kawaranu omoide

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
The dying breeze and my unchanged memories

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
Sotto misete ano koro no boku wa

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
gently reveal to me what I was like back then.

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Aa yume wo aishite hitori ni natta

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Ah, I thought that being alone

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
Sore de ii to omotta

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
and cherishing my dream would be fine.

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
Haruka na sora ni wa ima mo kimi ga iru darou

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
I wonder if you’re still there right now in the distant sky?

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Yasashiku ikiru yo afureru namida koraeta

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Now I lead a simple life, having suppressed my overflowing tears.

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
Mirai no melody ga shizuka ni yureru kisetsu

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
The melody of the future is in the quietly stirring seasons.

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
Aitai na itsu no hi ka... mattete

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
I want to see you again, and I’m waiting for that day.

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
Aitai ne boku wa mada humming boy

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
I want to see you again, but I’m still a humming boy.

24:19.980 --> 24:22.640
<b>Hey, Rokkun still hasn’t come. Isn’t he late?</b>

24:19.980 --> 24:22.940
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

24:22.640 --> 24:25.410
<b>This isn’t the first time he’s been late.</b>

24:25.410 --> 24:27.380
<b>That carefree tempo he has going is so annoying!</b>

24:27.380 --> 24:28.120
<b>Ah, here he comes!</b>

24:28.120 --> 24:31.350
<b>Ah, sorry. I was stuck in traffic.</b>

24:31.350 --> 24:33.990
<b>As if there’s any street in Tana
that would have a traffic jam!</b>

24:33.990 --> 24:34.990
<b>Rokkun, you liar!</b>

24:34.990 --> 24:37.450
<b>Now, now. I’ve only been late one or two times.</b>

24:37.450 --> 24:41.000
<b>It hasn’t been one or two times!
You’ve been late three or four times now!</b>

24:41.000 --> 24:42.430
<b>No, even more! This has to be the fifth or sixth time!</b>

24:42.430 --> 24:44.600
<b>Don’t worry about those simple little details.</b>

24:44.600 --> 24:48.170
<b>Don’t mistakenly think it’s five times. I’ll have
you know I’ve actually been late six times!</b>

24:48.170 --> 24:50.380
<b>If you want to joke around, if someone accidentally calls me Naruto (a fish-paste cake)...</b>

24:50.380 --> 24:51.640
<b>...I’ll just have to tell them I’m really Taruto (tart)!</b>

24:51.640 --> 24:54.380
<b>Next time: “The Constant Problem of Prioritizing.”</b>

24:54.380 --> 24:55.460
<b>If I had to choose</b>

24:55.010 --> 24:59.950
<b>The Constant Problem of Prioritizing</b>

24:55.460 --> 24:58.380
<b>between Old Lady Okaka (Okakababaa) or a pillowcase (Makurakabaa), I’d pick...</b>
